From 7688dc815dfe58c39103b48e23a83dacef5c10f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 06:46:03 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm: airoha: add AN7552 and AN7563 support

Add an AArch32 U-Boot proper target for the Cortex-A53 AN7552 family,
including AN7563 evaluation board defaults. Follow the supplied A7552
SDK handoff: the preceding stages initialize DRAM and trusted firmware.
Read the saved NP SCU capacity, fall back to board DT only for an unset
field, and propagate the detected memory bank to the kernel DT.

Reuse the EN7523 peripheral clock/reset layout with the U-Boot resource
ordering. Port the kernel AN7563 pinctrl data and add GPIO mux release
for the 38 GPIO lines. Enable the existing SNFI driver for SPI-NAND.

Add the AN7552 GDM1/QDMA0 copper Ethernet profile with its own PSE pool,
GDMP SRAM selection, fixed share threshold, flow-control mapping and
accounting selectors. Port the AN7552-specific PHY tuning, impedance
and analog calibration from the kernel and supplied SDK. Keep shared
REXT state local to one switch probe and propagate MDIO errors.

Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
